---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Wordmark from "../components/Wordmark.astro";
import wordmarkSvg from "../assets/generated/wordmark.svg?url";
import markSvg from "../assets/generated/mark.svg?url";
import tileSvg from "../assets/generated/tile.svg?url";

const files = [
  { href: wordmarkSvg, name: "wordmark.svg", note: "the logotype, one path per letter" },
  { href: markSvg, name: "mark.svg", note: "the L alone, cropped to its ink" },
  { href: tileSvg, name: "tile.svg", note: "the tile — favicons, avatars" },
];
---

<Base title="Brand — Luxe" description="The Luxe logotype, where it came from, and how to use it.">
  <div class="page">
    <section class="section section--head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Brand</p>
      <h1>One drawing.</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The logotype is not a font and not a traced image. It's a grid of terminal cells — three
          glyphs, the two half blocks and the full block — and those cells are the only copy that
          exists. The vector on this page is generated from them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Those three were chosen, not settled for. Every terminal with built-in box drawing
          synthesizes that range against the cell box rather than scaling a font outline into it, so
          the mark lands identically whether you have a patched font or the plainest monospace your
          distribution shipped. An earlier version cut its corners with the Powerline triangles and
          looked better on the terminals that draw those correctly — which is not all of them, and a
          mark that needs a fallback is the wrong mark to open with. There is no setting for it:
          one mark, everywhere, is the point.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="stage plate">
        <div class="stage__inner">
          <Wordmark shine class="stage__mark" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted stage__note">
        The light crossing it is the same one the terminal draws: 1.6 seconds to cross, then five
        seconds of rest. A shine that repeats promptly stops reading as light and starts reading as
        a strobe.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Files.</h2>
      <ul class="files">
        {
          files.map(({ href, name, note }) => (
            <li class="file">
              <a class="file__link" href={href} download>
                <code>{name}</code>
              </a>
              <span class="muted">{note}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">
        Each letter takes its color from <code>--luxe-wordmark-1</code> through
        <code>-4</code>, falling back to <code>currentColor</code>. Set them, or set nothing and let
        it inherit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--last">
      <h2>Please, and please don't.</h2>
      <div class="rules">
        <div class="rule">
          <p class="rule__head">Please</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Use the brass ramp, or one flat color, or <code>currentColor</code>.</li>
            <li>Give it room — at least the height of the <code>l</code> on every side.</li>
            <li>Use the tile where the wordmark would fall below about 100px wide.</li>
            <li>Keep the full stop. It is part of the drawing, and it sets the tone.</li>
            <li>Call it <b>Luxe</b> in prose and <code>luxe</code> in a command.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rule">
          <p class="rule__head">Please don't</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Set it in a typeface. It is drawn on a cell grid; no font has these letterforms.</li>
            <li>Add an outline, a shadow, or a gradient sweep of your own.</li>
            <li>Stretch it. The 1:2.2 cell aspect is the proportion it is recognized at.</li>
            <li>Capitalize it. The mark is <b>luxe.</b> and the product is <b>Luxe</b> — never LUXE.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .section--head {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .section--last {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .stage__inner {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--space-5);
  }

  .stage :global(.stage__mark) {
    width: min(100%, 34rem);
  }

  .stage__note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .files {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .file {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding-block: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--luxe-border-muted);
  }

  .file__link {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .rules {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(20rem, 1fr));
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .rule__head {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--luxe-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .rule ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--luxe-muted);
  }

  .rule li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
